# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# There was no such file, and `vercel --prod` from this repo therefore tried to upload FIFTEEN
# GIGABYTES and aborted part-way through. The CLI uploads the whole working tree — it does not read
# .gitignore — and this is a pnpm monorepo with a build cache, a git history and 724 MB of raw
# provider output sitting in it.
#
# The project's rootDirectory is apps/web, but the upload has to be the repo root or the workspace
# packages do not resolve. So the rule is: send the sources and the things the build reads from
# OUTSIDE apps/web, and nothing else.
#
# scripts/stage-media.mts reads exactly three places outside apps/web, and all three must survive:
#   storage/media        -> public/media
#   assets/3d            -> public/3d   (top-level .glb + manifest.json, gaps filled from placeholders/)
#   design-system/art    -> public/art
# Excluding any of those ships a store with no photographs, no 3D models, or no backplates.

# THE LOCAL DATABASE, SEARCH INDEX AND CACHE — 12.4 GB, and the entire reason the first deploy
# aborted at 15 GB. `infra/local.mjs` runs MySQL, MeiliSearch and Redis from here without Docker
# (see `pnpm infra:up`), so their data directories live in the working tree. The deployment has no
# database at all — it serves the frozen snapshot in lib/static-catalogue.ts — so none of this is
# wanted, and the scripts that manage it are dev-only.
infra

# Dependencies and caches — Vercel installs and builds its own.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.turbo
**/.turbo
.next
**/.next
.vercel

# History. Vercel builds from the uploaded files, not from git.
.git

# Staged copies of media that the build regenerates from the sources below. Uploading these ships
# every photograph twice.
apps/web/public/media
apps/web/public/3d
apps/web/public/art

# 724 MB of what the image-to-3D provider returned before normalisation. stage-media's `pick`
# already refuses it — nothing reads it back — and it is the single largest thing in the repo.
assets/3d/photoreal

# Generated models that assets/3d/review.json refuses. Kept in git as evidence, never served:
# stage-media only picks top-level .glb files, so these would be dead weight on the CDN.
assets/3d/rejected

# Captured brand pages, audit reports and run logs. Inputs to the pipeline, not to the store.
storage/raw
storage/reports
storage/calendar
storage/*.log

# Local scratch.
*.log
.env
.env.*

# Reference renders kept for comparison; not served.
generated images
